  "id": "COMPOUND:17351 - PROTEIN:2082",
  "verbalization": "Rel-Solamin is shown to interact with Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck, which is a key player in cellular signaling pathways. This kinase is subsequently targeted by two different compounds, Vitetrifolin F and Excisusin F, both of which are implicated in modulating the activity of Methionine aminopeptidase. The evidence suggests that Rel-Solamin may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the inhibition of Tyrosine-protein kinase Lck, which in turn affects the activity of Methionine aminopeptidase. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Rel-Solamin to Methionine aminopeptidase indicates a potential role for this enzyme in the regulation of signaling processes, possibly through the modulation of kinase activity. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Rel-Solamin and Methionine aminopeptidase, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
